{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"rich-moth","update":{"sessionUpdate":"tool_call_update","toolCallId":"exec:0#4ce62905d62247b4a41b34713edee61c","status":"in_progress","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"105:{\"id\": \"a-a55e8c909968\", \"at\": 1795425791833, \"subject\": \"persona:persona-051d2365a4d4\", \"predicate\": \"persona:reply\", \"value\": {\"type\": \"map\", \"v\": {\"text\": \"Harbor tides. Essential for navigation. Tidal atlases: thorough, yet often outdated. Coastal changes, dredging, and new charts can render them obsolete. Still, a valuable resource for those who use them. Worth noting that some modern digital platforms offer more up-to-date tidal data. For those who prefer traditional charts, a good tidal atlas can be a reliable reference. Invest in a comprehensive one, but be aware of its limitations.\", \"register\": \"clipped\", \"prompt\": \"set the topic to harbor tides, and tell me what you think about tidal atlases\", \"engine\": \"live-ollama:llama3.2\", \"fidelity\": {\"grounded\": true}}}, \"claimant\": \"persona:quill\", \"certainty\": 0.9, \"applicability\": 1.0, \"basis\": {\"kind\": \"generated\"}, \"supersedes\": null, \"links\": [], \"tags\": [], \"meta\": {}}\n108:{\"id\": \"a-f445b25a53b1\", \"at\": 1795425791834, \"subject\": \"persona:persona-d8df17c1cf35\", \"predicate\": \"persona:reply\", \"value\": {\"type\": \"map\", \"v\": {\"text\": \"Harbor tides! I just love how the ocean's rhythms can be so predictable, yet so full of surprises. You know, I've always been fascinated by those tidal atlases - those big, colorful books that show you where the tide lines are and when the high and low tides are. I think they're just so helpful for anyone who loves the water, whether you're a sailor, a kayaker, or just someone who likes to take a stroll along the beach. They're like a treasure map for the tides!\", \"register\": \"warm\", \"prompt\": \"set the topic to harbor tides, an