{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"rich-moth","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm deciding between two time-to-gate metrics: 2.352 seconds from the probe or 2.338 seconds from launch-check. The criterion specifies session start to gate pass, while the build measures boot to pass. Launch-check seems more appropriate as canonical launch evidence, despite the probe's timestamp being later. I'll use the 2.338-second metric from launch-check, citing its timestamp of 1795425815.1044414. For the scenario suite, I need to assign individual scores based on evidence."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T17:16:00.234241400+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"rich-moth","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe S-assertion-input score of .85 seems high given the transcript is thin, though it does show actual chat input. The S-template-need score of .9 is probably too high for a simple, fulfilled need. The S-candidate-ranking score of .7 is questionable because a `vhs tape` candidate should have failed an enum test but didn't due to a `_tool_of` bug, making the scenario's claim of \"failed/low evidence\" weak. The S-list-project score of .95 or 1 is good, fulfilling the project and artifact. S-personality-create score of .95 is also good, demonstrating coherence, though the portrait and voice are only procedural and immediate, not later work."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T17:16:08.712474900+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"rich-moth","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm scoring the background presentation at .85, noting it offers temporal attention via persona but doesn't clearly state completed background work. Competing tools score .95 due to two adequate tools for the same need. Restart recovery is .85, though the `before` check uses a fixed limit instead of actual row count. Exchange import is .85, with the package import below threshold and exchange media at zero. Deferred publication scores .95. Chat invocation is .85, despite a parser bug capturing too much as the topic; persona replies hallucinate facts. Focused need is .9, with the chat input filling a shallow need, though a bug affected the depth range."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T17:16:11.350089900+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"rich-moth","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm scoring the color scheme at .65 because while the theme change was observed, the scenario explicitly required driving the owner-facing selector control, which didn't happen; only API invocation was evidenced. The email commentary also received a .65, as it inaccurately critiqued a correct term, despite fulfilling the requirement for commentary. The status bar and portrait binding scored well, but the personality roster's .95 score is tempered by the fact it hits APIs, not DOM clicks, which the scenario wanted for operable control."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T17:16:14.266394100+00:00"}}}}
