{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"rich-moth","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe S-conversation-reset test doesn't explicitly cover the requirement for topic changes, though it does reset context. The S-context-display shows context but doesn't drive UI selection. The S-personality-editor saves updates but fails to persist responsibilities, as the `openEditor` function clears them and the patch doesn't include them. S-windows-launch uses a cmd script, which is acceptable for a program-like launch but not true packaging. S-close-terminate exits the process but has a long, non-graceful shutdown. S-speech-serialization checks ordering but not actual non-overlap, and admission timestamps are identical for queued items, though playback is measured correctly."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T17:16:17.528682700+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"rich-moth","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm assessing the scenario suite, noting that S-distinct-preloadeds has low Jaccard similarity with real Ollama registers, and some replies contain unsupported factual statements, though the scenario only requires distinct persona/style. S-library-browse scores well at .9, with good evidence counts. S-faithful-voice is problematic, scoring around .4 because its mechanism fails to produce source-accurate answers; it lacks source hits, has few grounded responses, and doesn't flag unsupported claims, with stale context overriding retrieval. I've identified 26 scenario needs, including S-conversation-reset, S-personality-roster, and S-color, and will now compute the average scenario suite score."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T17:16:20.524492400+00:00"}}}}
