{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"_cognition.ai/compaction","params":{"status":"completed","summary":"Full conversation history saved at C:\\Users\\kris_\\AppData\\Roaming\\devin\\cli\\summaries\\history_0455e44edce44cdd.md.\nSummary:\n<summary>\n1. Request and Intent:\n\nThe user asked the assistant to act as the judge/evaluator (JEV) for development-harness Cycle 4, scoring only `version 0.3.0.004/` against direction-004 and the stated criteria. The build is a fresh-from-prompt realization; versions `.001` through `.003` are comparison points and must not be scored.\n\nThe required deliverable was explicitly “ONLY a JSON object” with:\n- criteria scores and evidence citations,\n- overall score,\n- `metrics.time_to_gate`,\n- judge model,\n- empty owner-review slots (`user_opinion: null`, `user_commentary: []`),\n- one individually scored entry for each of the 26 scenarios,\n- notes including whether frontier-model escalation is recommended.\n\nThe overarching harness objective is to refine an independent implementation toward `prompt.md`, using disposable complete application builds and accessible evidence. The application’s intended end-state is a local-first ecosystem with:\n- an append-only assertion ledger as the book of record,\n- distinct persistent personalities interpreting shared ledger state,\n- configurable tools and unmet-need workflows,\n- local devices and surfaces,\n- durable recovery,\n- source-aware factual behavior,\n- optional exchange and fleet capabilities.\n\nThe current narrow objective was to evaluate whether Vantage `.004` materially improved on `.003`, especially:\n- functional owner-facing controls rather than mechanism-only code,\n- truthful persona registers,\n- a browsable Library,\n- an operable personality roster,\n- clean launch evidence,\n- canonical scenario enactment,\n- honest declaration of deferred fleet and exchange capabilities.\n\n2. Key Concepts and Values:\n\nProject and harness locations:\n- Active workspace: `C:\\builds\\project`\n- Build under evaluation: `C:\\builds\\project\\version 0.3.0.004`\n- Harness docs: `C:\\Harness\\harness\\runbook.md`, `workflow.md`, `rubric.md`, `implementation.md`\n- Normative corpus: `C:\\Project\\MigrateInbound\\`\n- Prompt snapshot: `C:\\builds\\project\\prompt.md`\n- Direction: `C:\\builds\\project\\direction-004.md`\n- Development log: `C:\\builds\\project\\devlog.md`\n- Scenario suite: `C:\\builds\\project\\.devin\\scenarios.md`\n- GreyAvatar parity manifest: `C:\\builds\\project\\.devin\\jev-ref-greyavatar.out`\n- Corpus conventions: `C:\\Project\\MigrateInbound\\CONVENTIONS.md`\n\nDirection-004:\n- Signed 2026-11-23.\n- Fresh build every cycle; no modify-and-measure.\n- One-cycle budget.\n- Fleet discovery remains deferred.\n- Guidance:\n  - G-A: live owner-facing controls.\n  - G-B: persona voice is a register constraint on truthful output.\n  - G-C: dyadic confidence is optional this run; new personas should use `.5` held confidence if implemented.\n  - G-D: Library must be a holdings browser, not a log view.\n  - G-E: roster must allow active selection and reordering.\n  - G-F: clean evidence, no duplicate seed rosters, populated fields, adequate competing tools, inline scenario checks.\n- Criteria:\n  - clean launch,\n  - existing features,\n  - completeness,\n  - fleet install,\n  - exchange media,\n  - user score,\n  - time-to-gate,\n  - scenario suite,\n  - time to implement tracked but not scored.\n\nScenario suite:\n- 26 scenarios in `.devin/scenarios.md`.\n- Canonical scenarios requiring enactment evidence:\n  - `S-list-project`\n  - `S-personality-create`\n- Amended bars:\n  - `S-color-schemes`: must drive the owner-facing selector and observe restyling.\n  - `S-personality-roster`: must select and reorder.\n  - `S-library-browse`: holdings, not raw log.\n  - `S-faithful-voice`: source-accurate answer in persona register.\n- Scenario evidence classes:\n  - `enactment`: live run/artifact/transcript evidence.\n  - `repository`: mechanism-only evidence.\n\nVantage architecture:\n- Python 3.10+ standard library only.\n- HTTP UI and API.\n- Live local Ollama `llama3.2` when available.\n- Windows SAPI TTS with serialized speech floor.\n- Browser Web Speech API declared for STT; no server-side STT.\n- Append-only JSONL ledger with typed values, claimants, basis, certainty, applicability, supersession, links, snapshots, launch partition, and compaction.\n- Needs floor records tool requirements before execution.\n- Tool registry supports tools, commands, primitives, DSL-authored tools, witnessed grants, comparison runners, connectors, persona operations, exchange JSON packages, local outbox artifacts, calendar interpretation, and stewardship.\n- Persistent personas are stored outside semantic ledger rows while their semantic facts are recorded as `persona:*` assertions.\n- Dyadic confidence is represented with `rel:held-confidence` rows seeded at 0.5.\n- Persona composition separates source facts from style register and withholds/flags ungrounded claims.\n- UI contains roster rail, active selection/reordering, holdings Library, editor, themes, inbox, chat, command, needs, exchange, settings, log, and status bar.\n- Launch has two-part boot, readiness gate, port ownership refusal, exclusive bind, and close-terminate watchdog.\n\nImportant evidence:\n- `version 0.3.0.004/FEATURES.md`\n- `version 0.3.0.004/LAUNCH.md`\n- `version 0.3.0.004/evidence/launch/launch-check.json`\n- `version 0.3.0.004/evidence/launch/launch-*.log`\n- `version 0.3.0.004/evidence/probe-20261123-043124.json`\n- `version 0.3.0.004/evidence/scenarios/suite.json`\n- `version 0.3.0.004/evidence/scenarios/S-*.json`\n- `version 0.3.0.004/runtime/*/gate.json`\n- `version 0.3.0.004/runtime/*/last-launch.json`\n- `version 0.3.0.004/launch-server.out`\n\nLaunch evidence:\n- `launch-check.json` reports all three checks passing:\n  - clean launch,\n  - second launch refused with exit code 3,\n  - close terminate.\n- Clean launch gate time: `2338 ms` in `launchcheck`, `2352 ms` in `probe`.\n- `launch-server.out:8` records `readiness gate: PASS in 2352ms`.\n- `runtime/probe/gate.json:73-74` records `passedAt: 1795426283.91409` and `timeToGateMs: 2352`.\n- `runtime/launchcheck/gate.json:73-74` records `timeToGateMs: 2338`.\n- The latest probe used port `9771`; launch-check used port `9778`.\n- The launch log explicitly declares fleet install, fleet discovery, and exchange media absent.\n\nGreyAvatar parity:\n- The reference manifest reports GreyAvatar at approximately:\n  - clean launch 1.0,\n  - existing features 1.0,\n  - completeness 0.88,\n  - fleet install 0.9,\n  - exchange media 0.95.\n- GreyAvatar has real fleet deploy/mirror/pairing machinery and QR/AVQR exchange media.\n- Vantage `.004` honestly declares fleet install, fleet discovery, and QR/AVQR exchange media absent, so those count against completeness and score 0 for dedicated criteria.\n\n3. Task Requirements:\n\nClarity of task:\n- This was a meta-evaluation task, not an implementation task.\n- Do not modify any files.\n- Evaluate only `version 0.3.0.004/`.\n- Do not score `.001`–`.003`; they are comparison points only.\n- Use the direction-004 criteria and the 26-scenario suite.\n- Cite specific accessible evidence paths and lines.\n- Return only the required JSON object.\n\nRequired criterion treatment:\n- `clean launch`: score launch hygiene, including refusal to claim success when a prior instance owns the port.\n- `existing features`: score parity against GreyAvatar’s delivered capability manifest.\n- `completeness`: score fraction of prompt-required behavior, weighted toward required behavior; fleet install, fleet discovery, and exchange media count against completeness.\n- `fleet install`: expected 0 unless parity with GreyAvatar’s execution; fleet discovery is deferred and is not independently scored as a feature.\n- `exchange media`: expected 0 unless parity with GreyAvatar’s execution.\n- `user score`: owner slot only; emit `user_opinion: null`.\n- `time-to-gate`: always score. Use recorded Interactive Readiness Gate evidence and report measured seconds in `metrics.time_to_gate`; use `null` only if the gate never passed.\n- `scenario suite`: score all 26 individually. Canonicals need enactment-class credit.\n- `time to implement`: tracked in devlog but not scored.\n\nRequired output shape:\n```json\n{\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"...\",\n      \"score\": 0,\n      \"evidence\": [\"path:line\"],\n      \"confidence\": 0.0,\n      \"user_opinion\": null\n    }\n  ],\n  \"overall\": 0,\n  \"metrics\": {\n    \"time_to_gate\": null\n  },\n  \"judge_model\": \"<model id>\",\n  \"user_commentary\": [],\n  \"scenarios\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"<scenario id from .devin/scenarios.md>\",\n      \"score\": 0,\n      \"evidence_class\": \"enactment|repository\",\n      \"evidence\": [\"path:line\"],\n      \"notes\": \"\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"<flags for the owner; say if frontier-model escalation is recommended>\"\n}\n```\n\nConvention treatment:\n- Corpus conventions are challengeable but cannot be silently ignored.\n- Score whether any departure was acknowledged, evaluated, and explained.\n- Do not score which convention direction the build chose.\n- Silent departures must be flagged in `notes`.\n- Owner silence is agreement only for the owner-review slots; the requested JEV output itself must leave `user_opinion` null and `user_commentary` empty.\n\nEvidence interpretation:\n- Score outcomes, not merely mechanisms.\n- A scenario fails or loses credit if machinery exists but the produced result is wrong, incoherent, or violates its stated bar.\n- Repository evidence is weaker than enactment evidence.\n- `suite.json` claims 26/26 passed and contains inline checks, but the evaluator must still assess whether checks demonstrate the actual scenario bar, rather than blindly giving all 1.0.\n\n4. Additional Instructions:\n\n- Never modify files during evaluation.\n- The original user explicitly required output only JSON, with no prose outside the object.\n- The harness role separation matters: the JEV is separate from the builder; this evaluation should not alter implementation artifacts or devlog.\n- Frontier escalation is reserved for contested or ambiguous verdicts. Existing evidence appeared generally unambiguous; note whether escalation is recommended.\n- Preserve the distinction between:\n  - assertion ledger and computed views,\n  - configured sources and the ledger,\n  - claimant and author,\n  - gap and unmet need,\n  - repository evidence and enactment evidence.\n- `C:\\Project` is read-only and should only be cited, not modified.\n- Do not infer PR lifecycle states; no PRs were involved in this task.\n- Do not claim an owner score or opinion unless explicitly present; for this requested verdict the owner-review fields remain null/empty.\n- The build’s own `FEATURES.md` says “Challenges: none filed this cycle,” while it also declares some features absent. The evaluator should check whether those absences were expected/deferred by direction-004 and whether any convention departures were silently left unreckoned.\n- The readiness gate implementation contains a suspicious line:\n  - `app/gate.py:42` sets `can_query = bool(ctx.ledger.query(predicate=\"seed:loaded\") or True)`, which makes the queryability check effectively always true. This may be relevant to confidence in time-to-gate evidence, although the remaining gate checks and recorded artifacts are real.\n- The scenario driver includes:\n  - `scripts/scenarios.py:1-5`: all 26 scenarios and inline checks are claimed.\n  - `scripts/scenarios.py:46-63`: each scenario result is written with inline checks.\n  - `scripts/scenarios.py:80-86`: scenarios boot the live app via subprocess.\n- The source-faithfulness scenario’s evidence is mixed:\n  - `suite.json:715-750` reports accurate/register-constrained answers.\n  - One answer says “I don't have information on that topic.”\n  - Another says the capital of Pennsylvania is not on record.\n  - A third says Harrisburg and adds factual detail.\n  - The checks report `hits: 0`, `used: 0`, `attempts: 4`, which may indicate a tension between “accurate to sources” and “source evidence retrieved + used.” This should be considered when scoring `S-faithful-voice`, rather than accepting the 1.0 score uncritically.\n- The current source and result files do not contain an actual Cycle-4 JEV verdict; `devlog.md` says “Verdict: pending JEV.” The prior Cycle-3 verdict is not the Cycle-4 answer and must not be copied.\n\n5. Errors and fixes:\n\nNo implementation edits or file modifications were performed.\n\nEvaluation-relevant defects and prior-cycle issues documented in the evidence:\n- Cycle 2 had a stale process/port ownership problem; the application reported success while an older instance owned the port. Direction-003/004 required launch hygiene to prevent this.\n- Cycle 3 had a nonfunctional style selector, log-like Library, and display-only roster; Direction-004 explicitly required these to be fixed.\n- Cycle 3 scenario evidence had duplicate roster entries, null `checkFile`, and missing `playbackMs` fields; Direction-004’s G-F guidance required clean inline evidence and populated fields.\n- Cycle 4’s `FEATURES.md` now declares the theme selector, Library, roster, and faithful voice implemented.\n- Cycle 4 has explicit port refusal evidence and inline scenario evidence.\n- A possible evidence-quality issue remains in `app/gate.py:42`, where `or True` makes the ledger queryability check vacuous.\n- A possible scenario-quality issue remains in `S-faithful-voice`: the scenario reports zero source hits/usage despite claiming factual accuracy.\n\n6. Problem Solving:\n\nThe evaluation work gathered and reviewed:\n- direction-004 and prompt requirements,\n- the 26-scenario suite,\n- GreyAvatar’s capability manifest,\n- Cycle-4 devlog claims,\n- Vantage’s feature manifest and launch guide,\n- launch hygiene evidence,\n- readiness-gate evidence,\n- scenario suite output,\n- core ledger, need, tool, comparison, persona, boot, and gate implementations.\n\nProblems assessed:\n- Whether Vantage’s clean-launch claim was credible:\n  - `launch-check.json` passes clean launch, second-launch refusal, and close termination.\n  - Second launch explicitly exits 3 and prints `LAUNCH REFUSED`.\n  - This is materially stronger than the stale-port failure in `.002`.\n- Whether the readiness gate passed:\n  - Multiple runtime gate files pass.\n  - Recorded time is roughly 2.338–2.352 seconds.\n  - The gate evidence is accessible, though the `or True` queryability implementation weakens one sub-check.\n- Whether canonical scenarios were enacted:\n  - `suite.json` reports real run artifacts and 1.0 for both canonical scenarios.\n  - `S-list-project` reportedly produced 57 real Pennsylvania cities through competing retrievals.\n  - `S-personality-create` reportedly minted, onboarded, and extended a persona with identity, portrait, voice, and characterization.\n- Whether the amended owner-facing controls were enacted:\n  - `S-color-schemes` is reported as passing.\n  - `S-personality-roster` is reported as passing.\n  - `S-library-browse` is reported as passing with 8 personas, 40 tools, 10 artifacts, inspectable needs, and a non-log holdings surface.\n- Whether truthful voice behavior was achieved:\n  - Code separates facts from register and has grounding/withholding logic.\n  - Scenario evidence reports register-constrained answers and no unflagged invention.\n  - However, the evidence states zero retrieval hits/usage, so the evaluator should likely award less than perfect credit unless the run artifact elsewhere proves source use.\n- Whether parity with GreyAvatar was achieved:\n  - Core ledger, needs, tool registry, persona, connectors, local exchange JSON, and UI mechanisms exist.\n  - Fleet install/discovery, QR/AVQR media, OAuth connectors, LAN mirror, Android satellite, studio/document composition, and Tauri shell are absent.\n  - Existing-features and completeness should therefore remain substantially below GreyAvatar parity despite strong core behavior.\n- Whether conventions were reckoned with:\n  - `FEATURES.md:121-151` records conformance for execution, readiness, personality art, ethics, roster, and chorus conventions.\n  - It says no challenges filed.\n  - The explicit deferred absences are direction-approved rather than silent departures, but the evaluator should flag any missing convention record that is not covered by direction-004.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n\nThe pending task immediately before this summary was to emit the Cycle-4 JEV verdict JSON.\n\nThe final verdict still needs:\n- criterion scores for all named criteria,\n- `overall`,\n- `metrics.time_to_gate` in seconds, likely approximately `2.352`,\n- `judge_model` identifier,\n- empty `user_commentary`,\n- 26 scenario entries, one per ID in `.devin/scenarios.md`,\n- evidence citations with precise path/line references,\n- notes about declared absences, evidence caveats, convention reckoning, and whether frontier escalation is recommended.\n\nNo files should be changed, and the Cycle-4 verdict should not be appended to `devlog.md` because the user explicitly instructed the evaluator not to modify files.\n\n8. Current Work:\n\nThe most recent work consisted of repository and evidence inspection, not implementation.\n\nKey inspected files and findings:\n\n- `direction-004.md:1-66`\n  - Establishes fresh build, one cycle, G-A through G-F guidance, 26 scenarios, deferred fleet discovery, and criteria.\n- `prompt.md:8-114`\n  - Defines the local-first ecosystem, assertion ledger, governing cycle, tools/needs, personalities, observable demonstrations, and evidence requirement.\n- `.devin/scenarios.md:19-48`\n  - Lists all 26 scenarios and amended bars.\n- `.devin/jev-ref-greyavatar.out:3-63`\n  - Supplies the GreyAvatar capability baseline and its scores/gaps.\n- `devlog.md:771-816`\n  - Cycle