{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"rich-moth","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI need to ensure all 26 scenario objects are included in the JSON output, keeping notes concise but specific. I'll carefully construct the JSON, validating for trailing commas and ensuring no prose exists outside the output. I've drafted the criteria and evidence details, noting specific file paths and line numbers for launch evidence, existing features, completeness, fleet install, exchange media, user score, time-to-gate score, and scenario suite score. I'll cite specific lines from various files for each criterion, prioritizing accessible paths with forward slashes and line numbers."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T17:17:03.638271700+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"rich-moth","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm noting discrepancies in evidence citations, particularly for the `lists` suite where a file exists but isn't referenced by line number, and for the `faithful` suite where evidence might be better sourced from artifacts rather than code. I also need to clarify that `assert` requires a real API call, not spoken input, and that low-confidence candidates for `candidate` are acceptable, though they lower the score. The `chat` feature needs better distinction, as its replies aren't source-grounded, though the scenario didn't mandate it."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T17:17:07.218655400+00:00"}}}}
